# наблюдение явной записью: локалы не публикуются (#flush-receiver-contract)
# Types is never called. Its implicit wrappers check the supplied places;
# their unpromised payload must not be read or stored into the filled data.
# Step 21.7 K2, S3: the record Types is written inside Build and launched by `Build\Types()` over its data
# parent(Types) = Build. Types holds only the reference declarations `@: p int` and `@: s A`: they are checked on
# their lines against the places of Build (p is a reference to int, s is a reference to A). No payload is read into
# the filled data and nothing is stored into it: Build keeps its prepared places -- p stays the reference to i
# (its dereference gives p_after 3), s stays A (s_after 7). Whether a local write took place is not concluded
# from the graph. The former record `call(data; Types\data)` still has the two positionals of [args, code]; the
# substitution of DATA is removed, and it answers 5 on this scene.
# Norm: the book #structural-call, the roles of data and code (#data-code-roles).
Observed:
    int: before 0
    int: after 0
    int: p_after 0
    int: s_after 0
end: Observed
Build:
    int: i 3
    A:
        int: v 7
    end: A
    @: p int @i
    @: s A
    Types:
        @: p int
        @: s A
    end: Types
end: Build
Main:
    Observed\before := 1
    Build\Types()
    Observed\after := 1
    Observed\p_after := \(Build\p)
    Observed\s_after := Build\s\v
